integ5 0073 = patches/glue5/0068-glm-mm-two-problem-decode-launches.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.
integ5 resolution: glm_mm_policy_host.zig keeps pdl5 0067's TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN test before this patch's test; cuda_mm.zig Kernels.load keeps `k.chain = Chain.read();` beside the TF_GLM_MM_TWO read.

glm cuda: two decode projections of one width in one glm_mm launch, each keeping its own K slices (T3 candidate 2, glue5)

- glm_mm.cu: glm_mm{16,4,6,8}_{16,32,64}t (MmTwo): x runs problem 0's column tiles times its slices, then problem 1's;
  each block is the block a lone glm_mm{B}_{BM} launch runs for its (column tile, slice): mm_kernel gains an `xtile`
  argument beside `zslice` (unset, the SASS of all 34 existing glm_mm kernels is unchanged, cuobjdump diff per
  function). glm_mm_reduce_two adds each problem's slices in slice order and rounds once, glm_mm_reduce's sums.
- cuda_mm.matmulTwo: launches them for two decode problems (rows <= 64, one width, splitK of each shape as `matmul`
  takes it, PDL as `matmul`'s matmuls, the reduce an ordinary launch); refuses (false, nothing launched) when the
  kernels, TF_GLM_MM_TWO (=0: off), the rows, widths, shapes or the scratch do not fit.
- cuda_dsa_block.prepareProfile (decode windows, shared windows and the MTP head): [q_a | kv_a] with the indexer's kw
  (both on the layer's rows, SK 8 and 8 at TP2), and q_b with the indexer's qb on the q rows (SK 2 and 4, sparse rows
  only). Codex's correction is kept: the problems are not concatenated into one N, so neither changes its K slices.
- cuda_state: a decode buffer's mm_part holds both problems' slices (twoPartBytes; the q_b + qb pair needs 128 KiB a row
  at TP2 against 64 KiB before: +1 MiB on the 16-row window buffer, +2 MiB on the 32-row shared one; prompt buffers
  unchanged); dsa_block.Scratch.mm_part_bytes carries the size (0 elsewhere: the two-call path).
- Exact: every output and partial is computed by the same block code in the same order; host test for the dispatch
  (glm_mm_policy_host.zig) and the scratch (cuda_state.zig).

